[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":2282},["ShallowReactive",2],{"page-\u002Fsql\u002F08-set-operations":3},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":2275,"extension":2276,"meta":2277,"navigation":168,"path":2278,"seo":2279,"stem":2280,"__hash__":2281},"content\u002Fsql\u002F08-set-operations.md","08 — Set Operations",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":2267},"minimark",[9,13,22,27,107,547,554,558,572,983,989,993,996,2263],[10,11,5],"h1",{"id":12},"_08-set-operations",[14,15,16,17,21],"p",{},"Set operations combine the ",[18,19,20],"strong",{},"rows"," of two result sets vertically (stacking), as opposed to joins, which combine them horizontally. Both inputs must have compatible column structure.",[23,24,26],"h2",{"id":25},"the-three-operations","The Three Operations",[28,29,30,43],"table",{},[31,32,33],"thead",{},[34,35,36,40],"tr",{},[37,38,39],"th",{},"Operation",[37,41,42],{},"Behavior",[44,45,46,62,74,88],"tbody",{},[34,47,48,55],{},[49,50,51],"td",{},[52,53,54],"code",{},"UNION",[49,56,57,58,61],{},"All rows from both inputs, ",[18,59,60],{},"duplicates removed",".",[34,63,64,69],{},[49,65,66],{},[52,67,68],{},"UNION ALL",[49,70,57,71,61],{},[18,72,73],{},"duplicates kept",[34,75,76,81],{},[49,77,78],{},[52,79,80],{},"INTERSECT",[49,82,83,84,87],{},"Rows present in ",[18,85,86],{},"both"," inputs, duplicates removed.",[34,89,90,100],{},[49,91,92,95,96,99],{},[52,93,94],{},"EXCEPT"," (a.k.a. ",[52,97,98],{},"MINUS"," in Oracle)",[49,101,102,103,106],{},"Rows in the first input ",[18,104,105],{},"not in"," the second, duplicates removed.",[108,109,111],"code-wrapper",{"language":110},"sql",[112,113,117],"pre",{"className":114,"code":115,"language":110,"meta":116,"style":116},"language-sql shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","-- All cities that appear in either customers or suppliers\nSELECT city FROM customers\nUNION\nSELECT city FROM suppliers;\n\n-- All cities, including duplicates (faster — no dedup)\nSELECT city FROM customers\nUNION ALL\nSELECT city FROM suppliers;\n\n-- Cities that have both customers and suppliers\nSELECT city FROM customers\nINTERSECT\nSELECT city FROM suppliers;\n\n-- Cities with customers but no suppliers\nSELECT city FROM customers\nEXCEPT\nSELECT city FROM suppliers;\n``\n::\n\n## UNION vs UNION ALL — the performance difference\n\n`UNION` (without `ALL`) removes duplicates, which requires a **sort or hash** across the entire combined result — O(N log N) or O(N) memory. `UNION ALL` just concatenates — O(1).\n\nIf you know the inputs are disjoint (or you want duplicates), always use `UNION ALL`. It's dramatically faster on large inputs. A common mistake is reflexively writing `UNION` when `UNION ALL` is correct, paying a hidden dedup cost.\n\n## Column Compatibility Rules\n\nFor a set operation to be valid:\n\n1. **Same number of columns** in both inputs.\n2. **Compatible types** in each column position (the database coerces where possible).\n3. Column **names** come from the **first** input — the second input's column names are ignored.\n\n::code-wrapper{language=\"sql\"}\n```sql\n-- OK: same column count, compatible types\nSELECT id, name FROM customers\nUNION ALL\nSELECT id, company_name FROM suppliers;   -- result column is named \"name\" (from first)\n\n-- ❌ ERROR: each SELECT must have the same number of columns\nSELECT id, name FROM customers\nUNION ALL\nSELECT id FROM suppliers;\n``\n","",[52,118,119,128,145,151,163,170,176,187,193,204,209,215,226,232,243,248,254,265,271,282,289,295,300,316,321,378,383,412,417,423,428,434,439,445,451,460,465,486,492,498,504,509,515,520,526,531,536,542],{"__ignoreMap":116},[120,121,124],"span",{"class":122,"line":123},"line",1,[120,125,127],{"class":126},"sdCPZ","-- All cities that appear in either customers or suppliers\n",[120,129,131,135,139,142],{"class":122,"line":130},2,[120,132,134],{"class":133},"svdQ7","SELECT",[120,136,138],{"class":137},"ssxIu"," city ",[120,140,141],{"class":133},"FROM",[120,143,144],{"class":137}," customers\n",[120,146,148],{"class":122,"line":147},3,[120,149,150],{"class":133},"UNION\n",[120,152,154,156,158,160],{"class":122,"line":153},4,[120,155,134],{"class":133},[120,157,138],{"class":137},[120,159,141],{"class":133},[120,161,162],{"class":137}," suppliers;\n",[120,164,166],{"class":122,"line":165},5,[120,167,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},true,"\n",[120,171,173],{"class":122,"line":172},6,[120,174,175],{"class":126},"-- All cities, including duplicates (faster — no dedup)\n",[120,177,179,181,183,185],{"class":122,"line":178},7,[120,180,134],{"class":133},[120,182,138],{"class":137},[120,184,141],{"class":133},[120,186,144],{"class":137},[120,188,190],{"class":122,"line":189},8,[120,191,192],{"class":133},"UNION ALL\n",[120,194,196,198,200,202],{"class":122,"line":195},9,[120,197,134],{"class":133},[120,199,138],{"class":137},[120,201,141],{"class":133},[120,203,162],{"class":137},[120,205,207],{"class":122,"line":206},10,[120,208,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,210,212],{"class":122,"line":211},11,[120,213,214],{"class":126},"-- Cities that have both customers and suppliers\n",[120,216,218,220,222,224],{"class":122,"line":217},12,[120,219,134],{"class":133},[120,221,138],{"class":137},[120,223,141],{"class":133},[120,225,144],{"class":137},[120,227,229],{"class":122,"line":228},13,[120,230,231],{"class":133},"INTERSECT\n",[120,233,235,237,239,241],{"class":122,"line":234},14,[120,236,134],{"class":133},[120,238,138],{"class":137},[120,240,141],{"class":133},[120,242,162],{"class":137},[120,244,246],{"class":122,"line":245},15,[120,247,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,249,251],{"class":122,"line":250},16,[120,252,253],{"class":126},"-- Cities with customers but no suppliers\n",[120,255,257,259,261,263],{"class":122,"line":256},17,[120,258,134],{"class":133},[120,260,138],{"class":137},[120,262,141],{"class":133},[120,264,144],{"class":137},[120,266,268],{"class":122,"line":267},18,[120,269,270],{"class":133},"EXCEPT\n",[120,272,274,276,278,280],{"class":122,"line":273},19,[120,275,134],{"class":133},[120,277,138],{"class":137},[120,279,141],{"class":133},[120,281,162],{"class":137},[120,283,285],{"class":122,"line":284},20,[120,286,288],{"class":287},"sJ6F3","``\n",[120,290,292],{"class":122,"line":291},21,[120,293,294],{"class":137},"::\n",[120,296,298],{"class":122,"line":297},22,[120,299,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,301,303,306,308,311,313],{"class":122,"line":302},23,[120,304,305],{"class":137},"## ",[120,307,54],{"class":133},[120,309,310],{"class":137}," vs ",[120,312,68],{"class":133},[120,314,315],{"class":137}," — the performance difference\n",[120,317,319],{"class":122,"line":318},24,[120,320,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,322,324,327,330,333,336,339,342,345,348,351,354,357,360,362,365,368,371,375],{"class":122,"line":323},25,[120,325,326],{"class":287},"`UNION`",[120,328,329],{"class":137}," (",[120,331,332],{"class":133},"without",[120,334,335],{"class":287}," `ALL`",[120,337,338],{"class":137},") removes duplicates, which requires a ",[120,340,341],{"class":133},"**",[120,343,344],{"class":137},"sort ",[120,346,347],{"class":133},"or",[120,349,350],{"class":133}," hash**",[120,352,353],{"class":137}," across the entire combined result — O(N ",[120,355,356],{"class":133},"log",[120,358,359],{"class":137}," N) ",[120,361,347],{"class":133},[120,363,364],{"class":137}," O(N) memory. ",[120,366,367],{"class":287},"`UNION ALL`",[120,369,370],{"class":137}," just concatenates — O(",[120,372,374],{"class":373},"snvgF","1",[120,376,377],{"class":137},").\n",[120,379,381],{"class":122,"line":380},26,[120,382,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,384,386,389,392,394,397,400,403,406,409],{"class":122,"line":385},27,[120,387,388],{"class":133},"If",[120,390,391],{"class":137}," you know the inputs are disjoint (",[120,393,347],{"class":133},[120,395,396],{"class":137}," you want duplicates), ",[120,398,399],{"class":133},"always",[120,401,402],{"class":133}," use",[120,404,405],{"class":287}," `UNION ALL`",[120,407,408],{"class":137},". It",[120,410,411],{"class":287},"'s dramatically faster on large inputs. A common mistake is reflexively writing `UNION` when `UNION ALL` is correct, paying a hidden dedup cost.\n",[120,413,415],{"class":122,"line":414},28,[120,416,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,418,420],{"class":122,"line":419},29,[120,421,422],{"class":287},"## Column Compatibility Rules\n",[120,424,426],{"class":122,"line":425},30,[120,427,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,429,431],{"class":122,"line":430},31,[120,432,433],{"class":287},"For a set operation to be valid:\n",[120,435,437],{"class":122,"line":436},32,[120,438,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,440,442],{"class":122,"line":441},33,[120,443,444],{"class":287},"1. **Same number of columns** in both inputs.\n",[120,446,448],{"class":122,"line":447},34,[120,449,450],{"class":287},"2. **Compatible types** in each column position (the database coerces where possible).\n",[120,452,454,457],{"class":122,"line":453},35,[120,455,456],{"class":287},"3. Column **names** come from the **first** input — the second input'",[120,458,459],{"class":137},"s column names are ignored.\n",[120,461,463],{"class":122,"line":462},36,[120,464,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,466,468,471,474,477,480,483],{"class":122,"line":467},37,[120,469,470],{"class":137},"::code",[120,472,473],{"class":133},"-",[120,475,476],{"class":137},"wrapper{",[120,478,479],{"class":133},"language=",[120,481,482],{"class":287},"\"sql\"",[120,484,485],{"class":137},"}\n",[120,487,489],{"class":122,"line":488},38,[120,490,491],{"class":287},"```sql\n",[120,493,495],{"class":122,"line":494},39,[120,496,497],{"class":287},"-- OK: same column count, compatible types\n",[120,499,501],{"class":122,"line":500},40,[120,502,503],{"class":287},"SELECT id, name FROM customers\n",[120,505,507],{"class":122,"line":506},41,[120,508,192],{"class":287},[120,510,512],{"class":122,"line":511},42,[120,513,514],{"class":287},"SELECT id, company_name FROM suppliers;   -- result column is named \"name\" (from first)\n",[120,516,518],{"class":122,"line":517},43,[120,519,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,521,523],{"class":122,"line":522},44,[120,524,525],{"class":287},"-- ❌ ERROR: each SELECT must have the same number of columns\n",[120,527,529],{"class":122,"line":528},45,[120,530,503],{"class":287},[120,532,534],{"class":122,"line":533},46,[120,535,192],{"class":287},[120,537,539],{"class":122,"line":538},47,[120,540,541],{"class":287},"SELECT id FROM suppliers;\n",[120,543,545],{"class":122,"line":544},48,[120,546,288],{"class":287},[14,548,549,550,553],{},"Type coercion can surprise: ",[52,551,552],{},"SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 'a'"," may coerce the integer to text or error, depending on the engine. Keep types explicit and matching.",[23,555,557],{"id":556},"order-by-and-limit-with-set-operations","ORDER BY and LIMIT with Set Operations",[14,559,560,563,564,567,568,571],{},[52,561,562],{},"ORDER BY","\u002F",[52,565,566],{},"LIMIT"," apply to the ",[18,569,570],{},"whole"," combined result and must come at the end. You can't order one input separately (parentheses around individual queries aren't standard, though PostgreSQL allows them with limitations):",[108,573,574,780,783,786,790,801,822,838,842,856],{"language":110},[112,575,577],{"className":114,"code":576,"language":110,"meta":116,"style":116},"-- Sort the combined result\nSELECT name, 'customer' AS kind FROM customers\nUNION ALL\nSELECT name, 'supplier' AS kind FROM suppliers\nORDER BY name;\n\n-- Limit the combined result\nSELECT name FROM customers\nUNION ALL\nSELECT name FROM suppliers\nORDER BY name\nLIMIT 10;\n``\n::\n\nTo limit *each* input before combining, use a subquery or CTE per branch:\n\n::code-wrapper{language=\"sql\"}\n```sql\n(SELECT name FROM customers ORDER BY name LIMIT 5)\nUNION ALL\n(SELECT name FROM suppliers ORDER BY name LIMIT 5)\nORDER BY name;\n",[52,578,579,584,607,611,631,640,644,649,660,664,674,681,690,694,698,702,739,743,757,761,766,770,775],{"__ignoreMap":116},[120,580,581],{"class":122,"line":123},[120,582,583],{"class":126},"-- Sort the combined result\n",[120,585,586,588,591,594,597,600,603,605],{"class":122,"line":130},[120,587,134],{"class":133},[120,589,590],{"class":133}," name",[120,592,593],{"class":137},", ",[120,595,596],{"class":287},"'customer'",[120,598,599],{"class":133}," AS",[120,601,602],{"class":137}," kind ",[120,604,141],{"class":133},[120,606,144],{"class":137},[120,608,609],{"class":122,"line":147},[120,610,192],{"class":133},[120,612,613,615,617,619,622,624,626,628],{"class":122,"line":153},[120,614,134],{"class":133},[120,616,590],{"class":133},[120,618,593],{"class":137},[120,620,621],{"class":287},"'supplier'",[120,623,599],{"class":133},[120,625,602],{"class":137},[120,627,141],{"class":133},[120,629,630],{"class":137}," suppliers\n",[120,632,633,635,637],{"class":122,"line":165},[120,634,562],{"class":133},[120,636,590],{"class":133},[120,638,639],{"class":137},";\n",[120,641,642],{"class":122,"line":172},[120,643,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,645,646],{"class":122,"line":178},[120,647,648],{"class":126},"-- Limit the combined result\n",[120,650,651,653,655,658],{"class":122,"line":189},[120,652,134],{"class":133},[120,654,590],{"class":133},[120,656,657],{"class":133}," FROM",[120,659,144],{"class":137},[120,661,662],{"class":122,"line":195},[120,663,192],{"class":133},[120,665,666,668,670,672],{"class":122,"line":206},[120,667,134],{"class":133},[120,669,590],{"class":133},[120,671,657],{"class":133},[120,673,630],{"class":137},[120,675,676,678],{"class":122,"line":211},[120,677,562],{"class":133},[120,679,680],{"class":133}," name\n",[120,682,683,685,688],{"class":122,"line":217},[120,684,566],{"class":133},[120,686,687],{"class":373}," 10",[120,689,639],{"class":137},[120,691,692],{"class":122,"line":228},[120,693,288],{"class":287},[120,695,696],{"class":122,"line":234},[120,697,294],{"class":137},[120,699,700],{"class":122,"line":245},[120,701,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,703,704,707,710,713,716,719,722,725,728,731,734,736],{"class":122,"line":250},[120,705,706],{"class":133},"To",[120,708,709],{"class":133}," limit",[120,711,712],{"class":133}," *",[120,714,715],{"class":137},"each",[120,717,718],{"class":133},"*",[120,720,721],{"class":137}," input ",[120,723,724],{"class":133},"before",[120,726,727],{"class":137}," combining, ",[120,729,730],{"class":133},"use",[120,732,733],{"class":137}," a subquery ",[120,735,347],{"class":133},[120,737,738],{"class":137}," CTE per branch:\n",[120,740,741],{"class":122,"line":256},[120,742,169],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":168},[120,744,745,747,749,751,753,755],{"class":122,"line":267},[120,746,470],{"class":137},[120,748,473],{"class":133},[120,750,476],{"class":137},[120,752,479],{"class":133},[120,754,482],{"class":287},[120,756,485],{"class":137},[120,758,759],{"class":122,"line":273},[120,760,491],{"class":287},[120,762,763],{"class":122,"line":284},[120,764,765],{"class":287},"(SELECT name FROM customers ORDER BY name LIMIT 5)\n",[120,767,768],{"class":122,"line":291},[120,769,192],{"class":287},[120,771,772],{"class":122,"line":297},[120,773,774],{"class":287},"(SELECT name FROM suppliers ORDER BY name LIMIT 5)\n",[120,776,777],{"class":122,"line":302},[120,778,779],{"class":287},"ORDER BY name;\n",[14,781,782],{},"::",[14,784,785],{},"(PostgreSQL allows parenthesized set operation branches; standard SQL and other engines vary.)",[23,787,789],{"id":788},"intersect-and-except-with-all","INTERSECT and EXCEPT with ALL",[14,791,792,793,796,797,800],{},"PostgreSQL supports ",[52,794,795],{},"INTERSECT ALL"," and ",[52,798,799],{},"EXCEPT ALL",", which keep duplicates based on row multiplicity:",[802,803,804,814],"ul",{},[805,806,807,809,810,813],"li",{},[52,808,795],{},": if a row appears N times in the left and M times in the right, it appears ",[52,811,812],{},"min(N, M)"," times in the result.",[805,815,816,809,818,821],{},[52,817,799],{},[52,819,820],{},"max(0, N - M)"," times.",[14,823,824,825,563,827,829,830,833,834,563,836,61],{},"Standard ",[52,826,80],{},[52,828,94],{}," (without ",[52,831,832],{},"ALL",") dedup to one copy. MySQL and SQLite don't support ",[52,835,795],{},[52,837,799],{},[23,839,841],{"id":840},"emulating-full-outer-join-with-union","Emulating FULL OUTER JOIN with UNION",[14,843,844,845,848,849,851,852,855],{},"MySQL and SQLite lack ",[52,846,847],{},"FULL OUTER JOIN",". Emulate it with ",[52,850,54],{}," of a ",[52,853,854],{},"LEFT JOIN"," and an anti-join:",[108,857,858],{"language":110},[112,859,861],{"className":114,"code":860,"language":110,"meta":116,"style":116},"-- Full outer join of customers and orders on customer_id\nSELECT c.*, o.*\nFROM customers c LEFT JOIN orders o ON c.id = o.customer_id\nUNION\nSELECT c.*, o.*\nFROM customers c RIGHT JOIN orders o ON c.id = o.customer_id\nWHERE c.id IS NULL;\n``\n",[52,862,863,868,883,917,921,933,960,979],{"__ignoreMap":116},[120,864,865],{"class":122,"line":123},[120,866,867],{"class":126},"-- Full outer join of customers and orders on customer_id\n",[120,869,870,872,875,877,880],{"class":122,"line":130},[120,871,134],{"class":133},[120,873,874],{"class":137}," c.",[120,876,718],{"class":133},[120,878,879],{"class":137},", o.",[120,881,882],{"class":133},"*\n",[120,884,885,887,890,892,895,898,901,903,906,909,912,914],{"class":122,"line":147},[120,886,141],{"class":133},[120,888,889],{"class":137}," customers c ",[120,891,854],{"class":133},[120,893,894],{"class":137}," orders o ",[120,896,897],{"class":133},"ON",[120,899,900],{"class":373}," c",[120,902,61],{"class":137},[120,904,905],{"class":373},"id",[120,907,908],{"class":133}," =",[120,910,911],{"class":373}," o",[120,913,61],{"class":137},[120,915,916],{"class":373},"customer_id\n",[120,918,919],{"class":122,"line":153},[120,920,150],{"class":133},[120,922,923,925,927,929,931],{"class":122,"line":165},[120,924,134],{"class":133},[120,926,874],{"class":137},[120,928,718],{"class":133},[120,930,879],{"class":137},[120,932,882],{"class":133},[120,934,935,937,939,942,944,946,948,950,952,954,956,958],{"class":122,"line":172},[120,936,141],{"class":133},[120,938,889],{"class":137},[120,940,941],{"class":133},"RIGHT JOIN",[120,943,894],{"class":137},[120,945,897],{"class":133},[120,947,900],{"class":373},[120,949,61],{"class":137},[120,951,905],{"class":373},[120,953,908],{"class":133},[120,955,911],{"class":373},[120,957,61],{"class":137},[120,959,916],{"class":373},[120,961,962,965,967,969,971,974,977],{"class":122,"line":178},[120,963,964],{"class":133},"WHERE",[120,966,900],{"class":373},[120,968,61],{"class":137},[120,970,905],{"class":373},[120,972,973],{"class":133}," IS",[120,975,976],{"class":133}," NULL",[120,978,639],{"class":137},[120,980,981],{"class":122,"line":189},[120,982,288],{"class":287},[14,984,985,986,988],{},"The first branch covers all customers (with their matching orders); the second branch adds orders with no matching customer. ",[52,987,54],{}," dedups the overlap.",[23,990,992],{"id":991},"using-set-operations-to-compare-tables","Using Set Operations to Compare Tables",[14,994,995],{},"Set operations are a clean way to find differences between two tables (useful for testing, syncing, or audit):",[108,997,998,2038,2040,2242,2245],{"language":110},[112,999,1001],{"className":114,"code":1000,"language":110,"meta":116,"style":116},"-- Rows in production but not in staging (missing from staging)\nSELECT * FROM prod.users\nEXCEPT\nSELECT * FROM staging.users;\n\n-- Rows in staging but not in production (extra in staging)\nSELECT * FROM staging.users\nEXCEPT\nSELECT * FROM prod.users;\n\n-- Symmetric difference: rows in exactly one of the two\n(SELECT * FROM prod.users EXCEPT SELECT * FROM staging.users)\nUNION\n(SELECT * FROM staging.users EXCEPT SELECT * FROM prod.users);\n``\n::\n\nFor large tables, this is expensive (sorts both sides). For diffing huge tables, hash signatures or a row-by-row join on the primary key with a `WHERE row IS DISTINCT FROM` comparison is often faster.\n\n## 💡 Tips & Tricks\n\n- **Performance**: default to `UNION ALL` — use `UNION` only when you specifically need deduplication. The dedup cost (sort or hash) is often the dominant cost of a `UNION` query, and most real-world `UNION`s are over disjoint inputs where dedup is wasted work.\n- **Idiom**: add a **provenance column** to set-operation branches (`SELECT ..., 'left' AS src` vs `SELECT ..., 'right' AS src`) to track which input each result row came from — invaluable for debugging \"why did this row appear\u002Fdisappear\" and for building audit-style diffs.\n- **Portability**: `EXCEPT` is standard SQL but Oracle calls it `MINUS`. `INTERSECT ALL`\u002F`EXCEPT ALL` are PostgreSQL-specific. If you need multiplicity-preserving set ops portably, use `JOIN` with `GROUP BY` and `count()` comparisons.\n- **Debug**: if a set operation returns fewer rows than expected, suspect an unexpected duplicate collapse — `UNION`\u002F`INTERSECT`\u002F`EXCEPT` dedup silently. Switch to `UNION ALL` temporarily to see the raw combined rows, or add a unique row identifier to make duplicates visible.\n- **Idiom**: when comparing two tables for equality, use `EXCEPT` in both directions rather than `count(*)` — counts can match while the row contents differ. `(SELECT * FROM A EXCEPT SELECT * FROM B) UNION ALL (SELECT * FROM B EXCEPT SELECT * FROM A)` is empty iff A = B (as multisets if you use `EXCEPT ALL`).\n\n## ⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas\n\n- **`UNION` dedup is global**: it dedups across the combined result, not per-input. If `customers` has `'NYC'` and `suppliers` has `'NYC'`, `UNION` returns one `'NYC'`; `UNION ALL` returns two.\n- **Column names come from the first input**: `SELECT a AS x FROM t1 UNION SELECT b AS y FROM t2` — the result column is `x`, not `y`. If you need a specific name, alias it in the *first* `SELECT`.\n- **Type coercion in set ops**: `SELECT 1 UNION SELECT '1'` may coerce to text or integer depending on the engine. PostgreSQL is strict-ish (it'll try to coerce, sometimes failing); MySQL is lenient. Keep types consistent across branches.\n- **`ORDER BY` column names must match the first input**: `ORDER BY` after a set operation references the first input's column names. If the second input named the column differently, you can't sort by that name.\n- **`NULL` comparison in set ops**: set operations treat NULLs as equal for dedup — `(1, NULL)` in both inputs is considered a duplicate and `UNION` keeps one. This differs from `NULL = NULL` being UNKNOWN in `WHERE` — set ops use \"is not distinct from\" semantics.\n- **`INTERSECT`\u002F`EXCEPT` precedence**: `INTERSECT` binds tighter than `UNION`\u002F`EXCEPT`. `A UNION B INTERSECT C` is `A UNION (B INTERSECT C)`. Use parentheses to make intent explicit.\n- **Set ops don't preserve order**: the inputs' `ORDER BY` (if any inside subqueries) is not preserved. The only `ORDER BY` that matters is the one at the top of the whole set operation.\n- **Large `UNION` can spill**: the dedup sort\u002Fhash needs `work_mem`; if it exceeds that, it spills to disk. For huge `UNION`s, increase `work_mem` or pre-dedup each branch with `DISTINCT` (which may let the planner use an index).\n\n## 🧠 Spot the Bug\n\nA developer wants to count how many distinct cities have either a customer or a supplier. This returns a much larger number than expected. What's wrong?\n\n::code-wrapper{language=\"sql\"}\n```sql\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM (\n  SELECT city FROM customers\n  UNION ALL\n  SELECT city FROM suppliers\n) all_cities;\n",[52,1002,1003,1008,1024,1028,1046,1050,1055,1069,1073,1089,1093,1098,1134,1138,1171,1175,1179,1183,1249,1253,1258,1262,1354,1439,1523,1614,1704,1708,1713,1717,1788,1856,1917,1938,1943,1948,1964,1969,1973,1978,1982,1990,1994,2008,2012,2017,2022,2027,2032],{"__ignoreMap":116},[120,1004,1005],{"class":122,"line":123},[120,1006,1007],{"class":126},"-- Rows in production but not in staging (missing from staging)\n",[120,1009,1010,1012,1014,10